---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Sidereal Cog" description="Learn more about Sidereal Cog">
  <section class="about">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About Sidereal Cog</h1>

      <div class="content">
        <h2 class="tagline">Engineered for the everyday</h2>

        <p>
          Sidereal Cog builds browser extensions that solve mundane problems. The kind of small frustrations you deal with every day but never quite get around to fixing.
        </p>

        <p>
          We're not trying to revolutionize your workflow or change how you use the internet. We're just making the annoying stuff less annoying.
        </p>

        <h2>Our Approach</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Start simple.</strong> Every extension does one thing well rather than trying to do everything adequately.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Stay practical.</strong> If it doesn't solve a real problem you've personally experienced, it doesn't get built.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Keep it clean.</strong> No bloat, no unnecessary features, no data collection. Just the tool, doing its job.
        </p>

        <h2>What We Build</h2>

        <p>
          Browser extensions for Chrome (and other Chromium browsers). Each one tackles a specific everyday problem:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Managing the small stuff that clutters your workflow</li>
          <li>Organizing information you reference regularly</li>
          <li>Streamlining repetitive tasks you do without thinking</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          If you've ever thought "there should be a simple tool for this," we probably agree.
        </p>

        <h2>Who's Behind This</h2>

        <p>
          Sidereal Cog is a solo developer project. One person building tools that solve problems they've run into, then sharing them in case they're useful to others.
        </p>

        <p>
          No team, no venture funding, no growth metrics. Just practical extensions, engineered for everyday use.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          For inquiries, collaboration opportunities, or questions about the projects:
        </p>

        <div class="contact-methods">
          <a href="mailto:contact@siderealcog.com?subject=Inquiry" target="_blank">
            <div class="contact-card card">
              <h3>Email</h3>
              <p>contact@siderealcog.com</p>
            </div>
          </a>

          <a href="https://github.com/Sidereal-Cog" target="_blank">
            <div class="contact-card card">
              <h3>GitHub</h3>
              <p>Sidereal Cog</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @import '../styles/global.css';

  .about {
    padding: var(--sc-space-3xl) 0;
  }

  .about :global(h1) {
    margin-bottom: var(--sc-space-2xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .tagline {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--sc-blue);
    font-size: var(--sc-text-xl);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: var(--sc-space-2xl);
  }

  .content :global(h2) {
    margin-top: var(--sc-space-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--sc-space-md);
  }

  .content :global(p) {
    font-size: var(--sc-text-base);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--sc-space-md);
  }

  .content :global(ul) {
    margin: var(--sc-space-md) 0;
    padding-left: var(--sc-space-xl);
    list-style-type: disc;
  }

  .content :global(li) {
    font-size: var(--sc-text-base);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--sc-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--sc-space-sm);
  }

  .content :global(strong) {
    color: var(--sc-text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-methods {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sc-space-lg);
    margin: var(--sc-space-xl) 0;
  }

  .contact-card {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .contact-card :global(h3) {
    margin-bottom: var(--sc-space-sm);
    color: var(--sc-blue);
  }

  .contact-card :global(p) {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
